From 95569d28a8b528b7f6e0cf0a3a8506c5e4b41402 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RepLog Dev <dev@replog.local>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 10:38:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/15] Coach Dashboard: unified 'Good morning' advisor on Home
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Assembles existing intelligence (recommendation + recovery + goals +
progression + plateaus) into one persistent advisor view. No new analytics.

- domain/coachdash/CoachBriefing.kt: pure builder that composes a single
  briefing — greeting (time-of-day), recovery score+directive, train line,
  focus (stalled lift/weakest muscle), progression line ('Bench: +Xkg next
  session'), estimated minutes, top-goal forecast, confidence.
- CoachViewModel: now also builds the briefing on load, pulling recovery
  (RecoveryAnalyzer), weakest muscle (latest DNA snapshot) and the top active
  goal forecast (GoalRepository). Injects TrainingDNARepository,
  BodyweightRepository, GoalRepository.
- ui/coach/CoachDashboardCard.kt: the rich Home card (greeting + recovery
  chip + headline + briefing lines + Start/Not-today + 'Why this plan?').
- HomeScreen now shows CoachDashboardCard instead of the simpler SmartCoachCard
  (SmartCoachCard retained, unused, for reuse). Reuses the existing accept /
  Smart Start / dismiss flow unchanged.

Verified: model+domain compile clean on kotlinc 1.9.22 (179 classes); 4
CoachBriefing logic tests pass in-sandbox (full train briefing, rest-day
suppression, no-recommendation greeting, progression fallback). All new
CoachViewModel deps are Hilt-injectable; no conflict markers.
